276 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 790 0 R
/E (In this Arduino program, a laser diode is connected to pin 2 \(LASER_PIN\), an LDR sensor is connected to pin 3 \(LDR_PIN\), and a buzzer is connected to pin 5 \(BUZZER_PIN\).)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
277 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 791 0 R
/E (The setup\(\) function runs once when the Arduino starts. It sets the laser as OUTPUT, the LDR as INPUT, and the buzzer as OUTPUT using pinMode\(\). The laser is turned ON initially, and the buzzer is kept OFF.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
278 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 792 0 R
/E (The loop\(\) function runs continuously. It reads the LDR sensor value using digitalRead\(\) and stores it in ldrState.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
279 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 793 0 R
/E (If the laser beam is continuously detected by the LDR \(HIGH\), the buzzer remains OFF. If the beam is interrupted or blocked \(LOW\), the buzzer turns ON to indicate an alarm.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
280 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (So overall, the system works like a security alarm that activates the buzzer when the laser beam is broken.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
