380 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 825 0 R
/E (In this Arduino program, a laser diode is connected to pin 2 \(LASER_PIN\), an LDR sensor to pin 3 \(LDR_PIN\), an LED to pin 5 \(LED_PIN\), and a buzzer to pin 6 \(BUZZER_PIN\).)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
381 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 826 0 R
/E (The setup\(\) function runs once when the Arduino starts. It sets the laser, LED, and buzzer as OUTPUT, and the LDR as INPUT using pinMode\(\). The laser is turned ON, while the LED and buzzer are initially OFF.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
382 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 827 0 R
/E (The loop\(\) function runs continuously. It reads the LDR value using digitalRead\(\) and stores it in ldrState.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
383 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 828 0 R
/E (If the laser beam is properly received \(HIGH\), both the LED and buzzer remain OFF. If the beam is broken \(LOW\), the LED and buzzer turn ON to indicate an alarm.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
384 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (So overall, the system acts as a security alarm that activates both LED and buzzer when the laser beam is interrupted.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
